{"kind":"action","text":"I write a replacement for the fixture in explicit pseudocode: `saveFrame(id, input) { scores = independentFloatArrayImmediatelyAfter(runSameMethod(input)); k = argmax(scores); history.add(HistoryEntry(copyValue(id), copyValue(labelFor(k)), floatValue(scores[k]))); } saveFrame(A, ownedInputA); saveFrame(B, ownedInputB); later { for (entry in history) render(entry.frameId, entry.label, entry.rawTopScore); }`. I use the old independent-array conversion for this version, with the array local to saveFrame and only copied ID, label and score values retained in history. I submit that edit and rendering path for the final A-then-B replay, requesting the immediate score snapshots and the two delayed rendered records alongside the unchanged references."}